WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:02.060
- [Narrator] Judging by the grandness

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:04.710
and length of this wall,
you could be forgiven

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:06.620
for thinking that it's in China,

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.103
but this is the Great Wall of India.

00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:12.686
(upbeat music)

00:00:17.709 --> 00:00:21.500
The Kumbhalgarh Wall is
located in Rajasthan,

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.250
roughly a 10-hour drive from New Delhi.

00:00:24.250 --> 00:00:26.860
Its remoteness has caused
this stunning location

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:30.610
to be relatively unknown, even to locals.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.860
The wall is made of
thousands of stone bricks

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:35.440
with artistic flourishes on top.

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.270
It has seven gateways and took
over a century to construct.

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:41.803
It was a place of refuge
in times of danger.

00:00:43.070 --> 00:00:46.520
The wall snakes through
valleys and along mountaintops.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:47.910
After the Great Wall of China,

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.400
it is the second longest
continuous wall in the world.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.730
It is 22 miles in length and surrounds

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:56.520
the fort of over 300 ancient temples that

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.840
were believed to have been
built in the fifteenth century.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:04.163
In 2013 it was declared a
UNESCO World Heritage Site.

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:08.350
A majority of the wall sits high,

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.930
serving as a lookout and
giving incredible views

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:13.460
of the surrounding
mountains and farmlands,

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.074
unlike anywhere else in India.

00:01:16.074 --> 00:01:18.657
(upbeat music)

